   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A home and its problems",
     "texto": [
      "**What it is like.** A flat can be **acogedor** (cosy) or **espacioso** (spacious). An **ático** is the top floor, with a terrace. It **da a** the street, **a** a courtyard or **al** sea.\n\n**Buying and renting.** The **inmobiliaria** shows you flats. The **inquilino** pays rent to the **casero** (landlord). All the neighbours form the **comunidad de vecinos** and pay the building's costs.\n\n**Doing it up.** First you ask for a **presupuesto**. The **albañil** works with walls and bricks; the **fontanero**, with pipes and taps; the electrician, with **enchufes** and cables.\n\n**What breaks.** **Se ha fundido la bombilla.** **Hay una gotera.** **Se ha averiado** the washing machine. Notice the **se**: things «happen to» people. **Se me ha roto** la persiana."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Hay que, dar a and the «se» of breakdowns",
     "texto": [
      "**Hay que + infinitive** says what is necessary, without saying who: **hay que pedir un presupuesto**, **hay que reformar la cocina**.\n\n**Dar a** shows where a window or a room faces: **da a la calle**, **da a un patio**, **da al mar**.\n\n**Se + verb** tells what happens to a thing, with no one to blame: **se ha fundido la bombilla**, **se ha averiado la lavadora**. With **me, te, le…** the person affected appears: **se me ha roto la persiana**.\n\nThe verb agrees with what breaks: **se ha roto la persiana**, **se han roto las persianas**."
     ],
